Tasks: Decomposition

Purpose:
  Define task decomposition engine rules, AI vs engine
  responsibilities, coverage validation, and dynamic task graph
  management.

Owns: ./

Scope:
  AI task proposal protocol
  Engine validation responsibilities
  Coverage matrix and orphan detection
  Dynamic task graph and plan versioning
  Research and decision-producing tasks
  Task type classification
  SDD pyramid branching hierarchy
  Branch naming and merge flow
  Branch lifecycle and deletion policy

Principles:
  AI proposes; engine validates.
  Task graph is not immutable — changes are audited.
  Requirement coverage is mandatory.
  Research tasks produce decisions, not code.

AIProposal:
  responsibilities:
    - understanding requirement
    - proposing decomposition
    - proposing dependencies
    - proposing acceptance criteria
    - proposing skill mappings

  limitations:
    - DOES NOT validate structure
    - DOES NOT enforce constraints
    - DOES NOT authorize changes
    - DOES NOT schedule execution

EngineValidation:
  responsibilities:
    - coverage validation
    - cycle detection
    - schema validation
    - policy validation
    - permission checking
    - scheduling

  rule: engine is source of truth for correctness

AIVsEngine:
  | Task                    | AI | Engine |
  | ----------------------- | -: | -----: |
  | Requirement understanding |  ✅ |      ❌ |
  | Task proposal           |  ✅ |      ❌ |
  | Dependency proposal     |  ✅ |      ❌ |
  | Coverage                | ⚠️ |      ✅ |
  | Cycle detection         |  ❌ |      ✅ |
  | Schema validation       |  ❌ |      ✅ |
  | Policy validation       |  ❌ |      ✅ |
  | Permission              |  ❌ |      ✅ |
  | Scheduling              | ⚠️ |      ✅ |

CoverageMatrix:
  structure:
    | Requirement      | Tasks    | Tests  |
    | ---------------- | -------- | ------ |
    | Reset password   | T1,T2,T3 | TEST-1 |
    | Send email       | T4       | TEST-2 |
    | Token expiration | T1       | TEST-3 |

  rule: every requirement MUST map to at least one task
  rule: incomplete coverage MUST produce INCOMPLETE_COVERAGE error

OrphanTask:
  definition: task with no requirement link

  allowed_types:
    - technical debt
    - refactoring
    - maintenance
    - infrastructure

  rule: orphan tasks MUST have explicit type justification

DynamicTaskGraph:
  principle: task plan is NOT immutable

  triggers:
    - research produces new decision
    - dependency invalidation
    - requirement change

  versioning:
    PLAN-100 v1:
      - T1
      - T2
      - T3

    PLAN-100 v2 (after research):
      - T1
      - T2
      - T3
      - T4

  rule: execution records which plan version was used
  rule: changes are audited via events

ResearchTask:
  definition: task whose output is a decision, not code

  example:
    TASK-RESEARCH-001:
      Goal: Evaluate Kafka vs RabbitMQ
      Output: ARCH-DECISION-001

  rule: research tasks MUST produce decision artifacts
  rule: research tasks MUST NOT produce source code

DecisionProducingTask:
  flow:
    Research -> Analysis -> Decision -> Implementation Tasks

  rule: decision MUST be recorded before implementation tasks proceed

TaskExecutionBoundary:
  rule: one execution = one task scope
  rule: agent MUST NOT switch tasks without formal TASK_SWITCH_REQUEST
  rule: files outside task scope are DENIED unless scope expansion is approved

Navigation:
  Tasks: @tasks.sdd
  ProjectTasks: @../project/tasks/INDEX.sdd
  Runtime: @../runtime/INDEX.sdd
  Orchestrator: @../orchestrator/INDEX.sdd
  Graph: @../graph/INDEX.sdd

Rules:
  [T-DECOMP-01] AI proposes tasks; engine validates structure and constraints.
  [T-DECOMP-02] Task graph MUST be a DAG — cycles are compile-time errors.
  [T-DECOMP-03] Every requirement MUST map to at least one task.
  [T-DECOMP-04] Orphan tasks MUST have explicit type justification.
  [T-DECOMP-05] Task plan is versioned — changes create new versions, not mutations.
  [T-DECOMP-06] Research tasks produce decisions, not code.
  [T-DECOMP-07] Task execution boundary is enforced — no scope switching without request.
  [T-DECOMP-08] Coverage matrix MUST be maintained for traceability.
  [T-DECOMP-09] Agent MUST NOT add signatures or sign-offs to task decomposition outputs.
  [T-DECOMP-10] Agent MUST NOT use emojis, icons, or decorative symbols in task decomposition output headers or titles.

State: +
